      "title": "Letterboxd review of Now You See Me 2",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Now You See Me 2\"] I think to truly open up to this franchise, you have to believe that this universe does not have music. Like, as a concept. They have magic tricks instead. Kids are posting \"omg hit tweet stream the new Ricky Jay.\" Directors are casting Criss Angel for a shot at the Best Original Trick Oscar. They got Jack Antonoff in the studio cookin' up new ways to hide a bird. If you accept that, everything else falls into place. Because the people of this universe treat these guys like they're the fucking Beatles– and frankly, they're under-reacting. If you suddenly saw Paul McCartney on the streets of Lo",
